      "id": "voice-leading-basics",
      "title": "Voice Leading Basics",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** harmony | **Difficulty:** 5/10 | **Time:** ~10 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Voice leading governs how individual parts move from chord to chord in polyphonic texture."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "principles",
      "title": "Principles",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Prefer small steps. Retain common tones between chords. Use contrary motion between outer voices (soprano down, bass up)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "classical-rules",
      "title": "Classical rules",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Parallel perfect fifths and octaves between independent voices weaken line independence. In trad, octave doubling of melody is normal; parallel fifths in two harmony instruments can hollow texture."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "session-application",
      "title": "Session application",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Bass moves by step or fifth when possible. Harmony on strong beats; passing motion on weak beats."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "entities": [],
  "entity_order": [],
